API proposal for Kestrel:

Note HTTP/3 always requires TLS connections but the feature still makes sense for other protocol translations.

```diff
public class Http2Limits
{
+ /// <summary>
+ /// If disabled (default) then the `:scheme` field for HTTP/2 requests must exactly match the transport (e.g. https for TLS connections, http for non-TLS).
+ /// If enabled then the `:scheme` field for HTTP/2 requests can be set to alternate values and this will be reflected by `HttpRequest.Scheme`. This can be used in scenarios like proxies converting from alternate protocols. See https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7540#section-8.1.2.3.
+ /// </summary>
+ public bool AllowAlternateSchemes { get; set; } = false;
}
public class Http3Limits
{
+ /// <summary>
+ /// If disabled (default) then the `:scheme` field for HTTP/3 requests must exactly match the transport (e.g. https for QUIC connections).
+ /// If enabled then the `:scheme` field for HTTP/3 requests can be set to alternate values and this will be reflected by `HttpRequest.Scheme`. This can be used in scenarios like proxies converting from alternate protocols. See https://quicwg.org/base-drafts/draft-ietf-quic-http.html#section-4.1.1.1.
+ /// </summary>
+ public bool AllowAlternateSchemes { get; set; } = false;
}
```
